---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MailtoCta from '../../components/MailtoCta.astro';
import { email, links, pageTitle, subjects } from '../../data/site';

const description =
  'Home automation that stays under your control: vendor-neutral, privacy-minded, usually Home Assistant on dedicated on-prem hardware.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle('Smart environments')}
  description={description}
  currentPath="/services/smart-environment"
>
  <div class="page-wrap">
    <article class="prose-measure">
      <h1>Smart environments</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Home automation that stays under your control: vendor-neutral, privacy-minded, usually Home
        Assistant on dedicated on-prem hardware.
      </p>

      <h2>For</h2>
      <p>
        Homeowners and small properties who want the house to work harder without handing everything
        to one consumer cloud.
      </p>

      <h2>The usual mess</h2>
      <p>
        Devices that do not talk to each other. Brittle DIY. Cameras and cloud accounts added
        without a clear architecture.
      </p>
    </article>

    <div class="card-grid card-grid--features">
      <article class="card card--static card--span">
        <h2>What we do</h2>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>
            Home Assistant on dedicated on-prem hardware (containerised, Postgres-backed). Cloud
            only where a device forces it.
          </li>
          <li>
            Mixed-brand Zigbee (ZHA) on open coordinators – lights, switches, sensors, shutters,
            water valves – not a single-vendor hub.
          </li>
          <li>
            Custom integration work when the shelf option is wrong (ZHA quirks, ESPHome, upstream
            contributions).
          </li>
          <li>Presence and occupancy that drive lighting and privacy automations.</li>
          <li>
            Everyday control kept deliberate: limited voice exposure, household dashboards, runbooks
            for ongoing operation.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="card card--static">
        <h2>NucBox (on-prem host)</h2>
        <p>
          The hardened mini-PC class of host we use for installations we build and operate. We do
          not sell this hardware and we have no OEM partnership.
        </p>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Encrypted disk with TPM unlock</li>
          <li>Tailscale-only administration</li>
          <li>No inbound ports from the public internet</li>
          <li>Encrypted nightly backups mirrored off-site</li>
          <li>Containerised Home Assistant and Postgres</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="card card--static">
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Local-first by default; every kept cloud dependency written down.</li>
          <li>
            Cameras via Frigate, with presence-aware privacy controls and network limits so footage
            stays local.
          </li>
          <li>
            Home network basics done properly: DNS, TLS on the LAN, mesh Wi-Fi, Tailscale for remote
            access, ISP/Starlink monitoring, off-site backups.
          </li>
          <li>Same host hardening as on the NucBox card.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We are not a certified alarm, medical, or life-safety installer.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="section prose-measure">
      <h2>Public engineering</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>
          <a href={links.haForumFieldNotes}>Home Assistant community field notes</a> (SONOFF
          roller-shutter switch)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={links.zhaDeviceHandler}>ZHA device-handler contribution</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={links.starlinkStack}>Open-source Starlink monitoring stack</a>
          {' '}
          and
          {' '}
          <a href={links.internetPi}>related upstream contributions</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Hands-on Home Assistant, Zigbee, and ESPHome work since 2024.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section prose-measure">
      <h2>First conversation</h2>
      <p>
        Bring the property type, what you already run, privacy priorities, and the one problem you
        most want solved. We map what must stay local, sketch a staged scope if it looks like a
        fit, and say so when DIY or another specialist is the better next step.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we continue under a separate agreement, typical outputs are architecture notes, an
        integration plan, a configured system in agreed scope, and an owner runbook.
      </p>

      <p>
        Email <strong>{email}</strong>
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Subject: <span class="mono">{subjects.smartEnvironment}</span></p>
      <MailtoCta subject={subjects.smartEnvironment} label={`Email ${email}`} />
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
